  "id": "rabinal_achi_music",
  "name": "Rabinal Achí (Xajooj Tun dance-drama music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Music of the Rabinal Achí, or Xajooj Tun ('dance of the tun'), a masked Maya Achi dance-drama of Rabinal in Baja Verapaz, Guatemala, that tells of the capture, trial and sacrifice of a K'iche' warrior; it is performed for the feast of Saint Paul in January and UNESCO recognises it as Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity. Its text was first written down in the mid-nineteenth century. The speeches and dances are accompanied by the tun, a wooden slit drum, and long trumpets. The maguaré card stands in for the tun and the horns card for the long trumpets.",
